#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# similarity_reduction

#% text
# `similarity_reduction(eq, u, [x, t], gen, f, z)` gives the ordinary differential equation for `f(z)` that the solutions of the partial differential equation `eq` invariant under its symmetry `gen = [xi, tau, eta]` (the generator `xi d/dx + tau d/dt + eta d/du`) satisfy, as `[ode, u(x, t) -> sol, z -> z(x, t)]`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The invariants come from the characteristic equations `dx/xi == dt/tau == du/eta` (solved by `d_solve`): the similarity variable `z(x, t)` and the form of `u` in terms of an arbitrary function `f(z)`. The form substituted into `eq` gives an equation in `z` alone.

#% item
# Generators with `xi` and `tau` free of `u` and `eta` linear in `u` (the usual case of point symmetries) and two independent variables; otherwise the result is `none`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% text
# Travelling waves of the Korteweg-de Vries equation, from the combination of the translations:

#% cell
similarity_reduction(derivative(0, 1)(u)(x, t) + u(x, t)*derivative(1, 0)(u)(x, t) + derivative(3, 0)(u)(x, t) == 0, u, [x, t], [1, 1, 0], f, z)
#% output
#= [-f'(z) + f(z)*f'(z) + f'''(z) == 0, u(x, t) -> f(x - t), z -> x - t]

#% text
# Its scaling symmetry gives the equation related to the second Painleve equation:

#% cell
similarity_reduction(derivative(0, 1)(u)(x, t) + u(x, t)*derivative(1, 0)(u)(x, t) + derivative(3, 0)(u)(x, t) == 0, u, [x, t], [x, 3*t, -2*u], f, z)
#% output
#= [-3*f'''(z) + 2*f(z) + z*f'(z) - 3*f(z)*f'(z) == 0, u(x, t) -> f(x/t^(1/3))/t^(2/3), z -> x/t^(1/3)]

#% text
# The scaling of the heat equation gives the similarity variable `x/sqrt(t)`:

#% cell
similarity_reduction(derivative(0, 1)(u)(x, t) == derivative(2, 0)(u)(x, t), u, [x, t], [x, 2*t, 0], f, z)
#% output
#= [-2*f''(z) - z*f'(z) == 0, u(x, t) -> f(x/t^(1/2)), z -> x/t^(1/2)]

#% subsection
# Scope

#% text
# The Galilean boost of Burgers' equation:

#% cell
similarity_reduction(derivative(0, 1)(u)(x, t) + u(x, t)*derivative(1, 0)(u)(x, t) == derivative(2, 0)(u)(x, t), u, [x, t], [t, 0, 1], f, z)
#% output
#= [f(z) + z*f'(z) == 0, u(x, t) -> f(t) + x/t, z -> t]

